  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR updates the user guide for the user-visible changes that merged after `v0.27.0`. It changes documentation and one site test only. It changes no code.\n\nThe guide is the documentation site (`site/content/guide/`) and the topic pages in `docs/user-guide/`. The decision record `docs/decisions/4439-guide-since-v027.md` gives the reasons.\n\n### Changes and the page that covers each\n\n| Merged PRs | Page and section |\n|---|---|\n| #4365, #4381, #4377, #3976, #3963 (tool library window, list, Tool tab, reserved pockets, rpm warning) | `set-up/tools.md` - Create and edit a tool |\n| #4103 (left-hand cutter) | `set-up/tools.md` - Create and edit a tool; `check-and-post/posting.md` - Post processors |\n| #4385 (Recipes tab) | `set-up/tools.md` - Recipes tab (new) |\n| #4188 (Copper C11000) | `set-up/tools.md` - Cutting data for wood and plastics |\n| #4240, #4251, #4276, #4280, #4402, #4271 (holder library, Holders page, user holders) | `set-up/tools.md` - Holders and profiles |\n| #4201, #4233, #4271, #4280, #4249, #4278, #4331, #4194, #4096 (tool components and stacks) | `set-up/tools.md` - Tool components and stacks (new) |\n| #4261 (`.camtools` version 8) | `set-up/tools.md` - Import and export |\n| #4414, #4206, #4164, #4184, #4251, #4114, #3922, #3985, #4186 (machine file keys, axes editor, spindle refusal) | `check-and-post/machines.md` - Mill |\n| #4270 (laser machine kind) | `check-and-post/machines.md` - Laser (new) |\n| #4139, #4246, #4070 (LN2W wire offset, Mark 21 header) | `check-and-post/machines.md` - Wire and sinker EDM |\n| #4382, #4373, #4367, #4363, #4185, #4184, #4169, #4166, #4289, #4195, #4163, #4162, #4196, #4198, #4170, #4299 (milling posts) | `check-and-post/posting.md` - Controller details |\n| #4248, #4387, #4242, #4172, #4158, #4114, #4395, #4161, #4164 (Heidenhain posts) | `check-and-post/posting.md` - Heidenhain DIN/ISO and Klartext (new); the Picomax 55 section no longer says that the Klartext post refuses cycles |\n| #4114 (`manualToolChange` manifest property) | `reference/post-processors.md` - Manifest |\n| #4136, #4008, #4014, #4416, #3832 (Contour Do not touch, trochoidal clean-up, ring merges, Chamfer arcs, Bore entry) | `operations/operations-2d.md` - 2D Contour, 2D Adaptive, 2D Offset, 2D Chamfer, Bore |\n| #4052, #3968 (DXF blocks, MPOLYGON refusal) | `set-up/setups.md` - Place a DXF profile |\n| #4314 (WCS flip refusal) | `set-up/setups.md` - Work offset |\n| #4199, #4210, #4217, #4191, #4223, #4168 (3D picks, Adaptive bore levels, rest in background) | `operations/operations-3d.md` - 3D Pocket, 3D Finish, Deburr |\n| #4084, #4174, #4018, #4321, #4074 (5-Axis Parallel picks, Rotary Flow sets, Swarf exit rise, icons) | `multi-axis/operations-multiaxis.md` - 5-Axis Parallel, Rotary Flow, Swarf, Rotary Contour |\n| #4098, #4296, #4277 (AC travel refusal, housing false refusal, playback) | `multi-axis/checks.md` - Machine check; Shank, holder and fixture collision; Playback on a work-turning rotary (new) |\n| #4246, #4097, #3617 (wire compensation, guide reach, closing overlap, centre slit, open-run skims) | `operations/operations-edm.md` - Wire Contour |\n| #3986 (Plasma Profile picks) | `operations/operations-plasma.md` - Plasma Profile |\n| #4267, #4183, #4117, #4105, #4013, #4140, #4237, #4108, #3987 (stock simulation and export) | `fundamentals/proving-out.md` - Stock simulation in CamCraft (new) |\n| #4364, #4366 (SolidCraft face names) | `docs/user-guide/solidcraft-camcraft-mcp.md` - Face picks follow SolidCraft names (new) |\n| #4187 (refusal names the field) | `reference/refusals.md` - Geometry and generation |\n| #4286 (stale caches after a generator fix) | `reference/troubleshooting.md` - Operations go stale after an update (new) |\n| #4319 (window capture failure) | `reference/troubleshooting.md` - Report a problem or request a feature |\n| #4232, #4221, #4216 (accessible names, field order, narrow pane) | `getting-started/keyboard-and-mouse.md` - Screen readers and field order (new) |\n| #4301 (local chat tools) | `automate/ai.md` - Ollama and offline-only mode |\n\n### Already in the guide (no new text)\n\n- Theme tokens: #4208, #4073, #4072, #3993, #3992 (`docs/user-guide/themes.md`).\n- MCP idle timeout: #4190 (`automate/mcp.md`, `docs/user-guide/start-options.md`).\n- The `edm/sinker` example: #4409 (`operations/operations-edm.md`).\n- The LN2W post and constant taper: #4065, #4171 (`check-and-post/machines.md`).\n- The Agie post name and reentrant openings: #4022, #4040.\n- The MCP tool component tools: #4268 (`automate/mcp.md`).\n\n### Internal (no guide text)\n\n- #4397 (`camcraft-ui-kit` crate, no visible change).\n- #4388, #4333, #4197 (gate and xtask).\n- #4361 (Klartext reader in `camcraft-gcode`; no app caller yet).\n- #4323 (mesh bodies for tool components; no UI or MCP path yet).\n\n## Cause\n\nThe guide did not describe the changes that merged after `v0.27.0`. The Klartext section also said that the post refuses drilling and tapping cycles, and the Rotary Flow section said that it needs two chains in the same direction. Both statements were wrong after #4395 and #4018.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `site/tests/test_release_028_guide.py` (20 tests). It asserts the key facts of each change in its section.\n- Red before the change: on `upstream/main` pages the pin has 143 failures (`FAILED (failures=143)`).\n- Green after the change: `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -p 'test_release_028_guide.py'` gives `OK`.\n- Mutation: the pin was run against the old pages in a clean `upstream/main` worktree (red), then against the new pages (green).\n- Full site suite: `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests` with Zola on `PATH`. The navigation, link and anchor tests pass. 28 failures remain. The same 28 fail on unchanged `upstream/main` (search query browser tests, two icon drifts, and bold-label checks of the two 4-axis tutorials). This PR fixes one failure that was on `main`: `test_manifest_properties_have_reference_rows` (the missing `manualToolChange` row).\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` plans 0 steps: nothing in `crates/` changed.\n- Clippy: not run. No crate changed.\n- Heavy lanes and the light lane: not run. No code changed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. This PR changes no code, so no recorded program can change. The example catalog suites were not run for this reason.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The text was checked against the PR bodies and the UI strings in `crates/ui/src`. It was not checked in the running app.\n- No screenshots: this is a prose change, and a PR does not change snapshot PNGs.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nSome open PRs change the same pages in other sections. Whichever merges second refreshes:\n\n- `automate/mcp.md`: this PR does not change it.\n- `operations/operations-2d.md`: #4316, #4173, #3103 (Drill, Chamfer leads, Bore Helical strategy). #3103 adds a Bore Helical strategy, and this PR describes the Bore helix entry of #3832. Read the two together at the refresh.\n- `operations/operations-3d.md`: #4410.\n- `multi-axis/operations-multiaxis.md`: #4429, #4408.\n- `operations/operations-edm.md`: #4424.\n- `check-and-post/machines.md`: #4312, #4288, #4263.\n- `reference/refusals.md`: #3103.\n\nThe writer record is https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4439#issuecomment-7227952973.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: none (docs only)\n\nFixes #4439\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
